      "stimulus": "The Legend of Lake Toba\n\nOnce upon a time in North Sumatra, there lived a poor farmer named Toba. One day, he caught a beautiful golden fish. The fish magically turned into a beautiful woman. She agreed to marry Toba on one condition: he must never reveal her past as a fish.\n\nThey lived happily and had a son named Samosir. Samosir was a lazy boy who loved to eat. One day, Toba asked Samosir to deliver lunch to the field. Instead, Samosir ate most of it. Toba was furious and shouted, “You, son of a fish!”\n\nHearing that, his wife was heartbroken. She had been betrayed. She cried and told Samosir to run to the hill. Suddenly, heavy rain fell, and the valley turned into a huge lake, now known as Lake Toba, with Samosir Island in the middle.\n\nMoral: Keep your promise and control your anger."
